In server/src/overview.rs, replace the body `todo!("unit o6")` of fn progress with the real code. Keep its signature and doc comment exactly. Spec: build a serde_json object with json!. Tasks = rows with kind == "task" (goals and milestones are not counted).
- "done": tasks with state "done"; "total": number of tasks;
- "running": state "running"; "needsYou": state "needs_input", "failed" or "refused"; "inReview": state "in_review" (all as numbers);
- "goals": for each row with kind == "goal", in row order, whose tasks (tasks with parent_id == goal.id) are not empty: {"title": goal title, "done": its done tasks, "total": its tasks};
- "next": up to 3 tasks with state "queued", each {"id", "title", "ready"}. A queued task is ready when every pair (task_id, depends_on) in `deps` with task_id == its id has a depends_on task whose state is "done" (a depends_on id not in rows counts as done). Ready tasks come first, then the not-ready ones, each group in row order; take the first 3.
Use a HashMap<&str, &str> from id to state for the dependency lookup.
Change nothing else in the file; the other functions keep their todo!() until their own job.
